CORE
main.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ b is reachable: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
main writes p = &b and then reads q, which the thread may have copied from p
in between: the lookup of q in the first run lacked the thread's value (the
thread is executed later), so symbolic execution is repeated.
